{
  "_comment": [
    "A curated sample of real DCS `object_type` strings, used by",
    "test_object_model.py::test_coverage_floor_against_real_type_sample to",
    "measure perception.object_model's keyword-table coverage against real",
    "data instead of guessed strings, and to catch a silent regression.",
    "",
    "Each entry's `expected_op_class` is what perception.object_model.profile_for",
    "should currently return for that real type (null means the fallback/",
    "DEFAULT_OP_CLASS case is the *correct*, expected outcome for this type).",
    "",
    "`bucket` classifies *why* -- used to compute a coverage floor on the",
    "bucket that actually matters (`ground`: real DCS ground-domain types --",
    "combat vehicles/systems and non-combat ground objects (statics, support",
    "equipment, radars, structures) alike, i.e. everything the naked-eye",
    "channel could plausibly see and report as a ground contact -- this",
    "module targets) instead of one blended percentage across everything,",
    "which is exactly the metric that hid this module's original ground-unit",
    "gap (see aircraft-layer/research/2026-09-09-object-model-keyword-",
    "coverage.md's Addendum): 'ship' (OP_SHIP, its own already-covered",
    "category, not a 'ground unit'); 'air' (aircraft/helicopters/UAVs,",
    "deliberately deferred, must stay at fallback); 'wwii' (ED's",
    "'Old ...'-prefixed reporting names, deliberately excluded even when a",
    "modern-unit keyword like 'truck' would otherwise also match -- see",
    "object_model.py's WWII-prefix guard); 'ground' (everything else --",
    "the coverage floor applies to this bucket only).",
    "",
    "**The `ground` bucket is a full enumeration of the real 'ground' domain,",
    "not a sample.** Every one of the 595 real `dcs_object_type` rows in",
    "src/perception/data/dcs_type_to_reporting_name.tsv was independently",
    "categorized (ship: via profile_for's own OP_SHIP result; wwii: reporting",
    "name starts with 'old '; air: reporting name matches a word-boundary-",
    "safe aircraft-designation keyword list -- fixed-wing/rotary/UAV type",
    "codes and names, e.g. 'f-16', 'mi-24', 'su-27', 'mq-9'; ground:",
    "everything left over) by a script, independent of whether",
    "perception.object_model currently classifies each type -- this is what",
    "makes the coverage number below a real measurement rather than the",
    "defect this fixture used to have (every prior 'ground' entry was",
    "hand-picked from types that already classified, so the floor could",
    "never fail). There used to be a separate 'ground_deferred' bucket for",
    "real ground/support types this module deliberately hasn't attempted to",
    "classify (towed AA/mortar pieces, SAM-system radars/launchers beyond",
    "IRIS-T, static structures, airfield support equipment) -- folded into",
    "'ground' with `expected_op_class: null`, since 'a real ground type we",
    "haven't classified yet' is exactly what the coverage metric is supposed",
    "to measure, not a reason to exclude it from the denominator.",
    "",
    "Measured when this fixture was built: 190/316 ground types classified",
    "(~60.1%). See test_object_model.py's `_MIN_GROUND_COVERAGE_FRACTION`",
    "for how this number is used as a regression floor, not a target.",
    "",
    "`ship`/`wwii`/`air` remain small hand-picked regression-guard samples",
    "(unchanged by this fixture rebuild) -- see object_model.py's own",
    "docstrings for why full enumeration isn't needed there (ship is also",
    "fully enumerable and was already committed in full; wwii/air are",
    "out-of-scope categories where the only thing worth guarding is 'stays",
    "at fallback', not a coverage number).",
    "",
    "Individual type-name strings only (no reporting names, no full extracted",
    "table -- the full table itself is committed at",
    "src/perception/data/dcs_type_to_reporting_name.tsv) -- see",
    "aircraft-layer/research/2026-09-09-object-model-keyword-coverage.md for",
    "the source (ED's HelperAI_reporting_names.lua, 595 entries total)."
  ],
